                # scale, so `var p: *i64 = &nodes;` — the canonical address-of idiom — tripped
                # `assigning non-pointer to typed pointer`, the compiler warning about the one
                # expression form that cannot possibly be a non-pointer.
                # ⚠ Scale 1 (BYTE-addressed), deliberately, not 8. Pointer arithmetic in this
                # tree is written in BYTES at the source level (`&nodes + i * 16`), and
                # EPTR_SCALE multiplies the addend by the scale — so any value above 1 would
                # silently re-scale every existing `&x + n` site and change what compiled code
